From: pas7std co-op <coop@pas7std.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH 0007/0007] npc: optional loadout override for a native NPC spawn

buildNpcDefinition(profileID) always took the loadout from the profile row, so a
caller could not fit a real authored loadout row for a profile whose row points
at the retail empty loadout (retail keeps NPC stats on the type dogma record).
Every pirate frigate/cruiser/battleship profile therefore resolved to zero
modules, while the profile's own `*_loadout` row (a real turret and its
compatible charge, already in the static tables) was never reachable.

An optional options.loadoutID is threaded from spawnBatchInSystem through
resolveNpcSpawnPlan into every definition builder and the definition cache. It
selects the named npcLoadouts row for the profiles this plan selects; a missing
row still fails as NPC_DEFINITION_INCOMPLETE instead of falling back silently.
Without the option the profile's own loadoutID is used exactly as before, so
retail behaviour is unchanged.

Upstream base: c3ea396b6761a0ed3e71ad5b8dd7507f9ae6d69f
Local overlay: integration/* is NOT part of this patch series.
